{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/gaqh81","slide":1,"text":"Hello. Today I will show how I matched sources in the 7DT COSMOS1 data. This catalog is one step toward testing redshift estimates. I started with 20 separate band catalogs. I found and measured sources in each band. After quality cuts, I used 78,882 detections from the shared area. I first linked the 7DT detections across bands. Then I compared the new 7DT catalog with FINALCAT.\n\nSource: presentation/2026-10-02/matching_presentation_plan.md; output/COSMOS1/singlebandphot/matching/figures/singleband_input_summary.png."}
